  "title": "Carol S NDE 6410",
  "date": "1971",
  "content": "I suddenly became very sick. My mother took me to my grandmother’s house, which was nearby. When we got in her front yard, I heard a loud buzzing in my ear that got louder and louder, and then I fainted. I felt fine again, no longer sick. In fact, I felt wonderful. I never knew what happiness was before that moment. The joy was unbelievable. Then I became aware of a disturbance below me: my step-grandfather slapping my face, trying to revive me. My grandmother was hysterically screaming, ‘she's dead, she's dead!’ My mother began to shake me, screaming, ‘she's not dead!’ All the while this was going on, I felt at peace. It was as if I was separated from them and in my own little la-la land, but yet I was aware of what was happening. It was like the bible says, ‘joy unspeakable and full of glory’. Their agony and grief did not disturb my peace. I stopped paying attention to them for a while. I just looked around. Everything looked beautiful. All of a sudden, I felt a thud. I felt so sick again. I felt very angry that they made me come back.",
